---
import JournalArticle from '../../components/JournalArticle.astro';
const title='An AI-built 3D Diwali greeting you can make your own';
const description='A custom personalised 3D Diwali greeting tool built with AI from Shubham Shinde’s concept, with draggable objects, day and night scenes, fireworks, and a flip card.';
const poster='assets/journal/diwali/greeting-night.jpg';
---
<JournalArticle section="experiments" readTime="1 min read" slug="happy-diwali-3d-card" title={title} description={description} shareImage={poster} shareAlt="Happy Diwali in an interactive 3D scene filled with diyas, kandils, marigolds and lotuses" projectUrl="/experiments/happy-diwali-3d/" projectLabel="Make your own Happy Diwali card" keywords={['AI-assisted design','AI-generated 3D models','interactive Diwali greeting card','creative technology','Three.js project']}>
  <figure class="journal-window"><a href="/experiments/happy-diwali-3d/" aria-label="Open the tool"><img src="/assets/experiments/diwali-3d-ui.jpg" alt="The live Happy Diwali 3D greeting with diyas, kandils, marigolds and lotuses around large greeting type" width="1440" height="900" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></a><figcaption>The Happy Diwali greeting running in the browser.</figcaption></figure>
  <section class="journal-copy">
    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p>An interactive 3D Diwali greeting that runs in the browser. Explore a scene of diyas, kandils, marigolds and lotuses, then flip it over and turn it into a card for someone.</p>
    <p>I wrote the concept prompt and AI built the experience; the 3D models were generated with Tripo and optimised by me.</p>
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ol class="journal-steps">
      <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v18M3 12h18M9 6l3-3 3 3M9 18l3 3 3-3M6 9l-3 3 3 3M18 9l3 3-3 3"/></svg><div><b>Explore the scene</b><span>Drag the diyas and flowers, and turn the whole scene.</span></div></li>
      <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 14.5A8 8 0 1 1 9.5 4a6.5 6.5 0 0 0 10.5 10.5z"/></svg><div><b>Switch day and night</b><span>At night, tap the sky for fireworks.</span></div></li>
      <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="5" width="16" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M8 10h8M8 14h5"/></svg><div><b>Flip the card</b><span>Write the names and your own message.</span></div></li>
      <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v12M7 9l5-5 5 5M5 14v6h14v-6"/></svg><div><b>Share it</b><span>Your message and layout are saved in your browser.</span></div></li>
    </ol>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/Fakerplay/diwali-cards" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Browse the Diwali Cards source on GitHub</a></p>
  </section>
</JournalArticle>
